#################################################################
# Curated description-record families
#################################################################

srd521:ConditionDefinition
  a cat:Kind ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Description ;
  rdfs:label "Condition definition"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A condition as the SRD 5.2.1 edition defines it, carrying the edition's prose and one row for each effect the condition imposes. It is rules-package data; it is not a claim that any live creature or character currently has the condition."@en .

srd521:ConditionEffect
  a cat:Kind ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Description ;
  rdfs:label "Condition effect"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "One effect that a condition imposes, taken row by row from the edition's prose for that condition. Where the effect takes a whole family of actions away (a condition that forbids attacking, for instance), the row records that withdrawal as data; the row does not itself apply the effect to anyone."@en .

srd521:D20SkillRule
  a cat:Kind ;
  cat:specializes par:DecisionRule ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Description ;
  rdfs:label "D20 skill rule"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A curated rule row linking a skill to its default ability and D20 test action-type."@en .

srd521:ItemActionOption
  a cat:Kind ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Description ;
  rdfs:label "Item action option"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A row from the edition's equipment tables stating that an item presents an action option, such as a melee attack or a thrown attack with a weapon. It names the kind of D20 test that option would use, as data; it does not authorize anyone to take the action in play."@en .

srd521:SpellDefinition
  a cat:Kind ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Description ;
  rdfs:label "Spell definition"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A spell as the SRD 5.2.1 edition defines it, held as reusable rules data. It is not a prepared spell, a spell slot, a commitment to cast, or the resolution of a spell's effect."@en .

srd521:SpellClassAvailability
  a cat:Kind ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Description ;
  rdfs:label "Spell class availability"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A row stating that a character class's spell list in the SRD 5.2.1 edition includes a spell. It records a table fact and nothing more; it is not a class package, a preparation rule, a spell-slot rule, or a claim about any character's known or prepared spells."@en .

srd521:SpellExpression
  a cat:Kind ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Description ;
  rdfs:label "Spell expression"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A damage or healing quantity taken from a spell's description in the edition, recorded as a dice expression or a fixed amount. It preserves the number as data; it does not encode the spell's effect or how that effect resolves."@en .

srd521:AreaOfEffectShape
  a cat:Kind ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Description ;
  rdfs:label "Area-of-effect shape"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The shape of a spell's area of effect as the SRD 5.2.1 edition states it, such as a sphere, cone, cube, line, or cylinder. It is reusable rules data describing the shape only; which creatures and places a live casting actually takes in is not settled by this record but adjudicated at the table against the scene's geometry."@en .

srd521:WeaponPropertyDefinition
  a cat:Kind ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Description ;
  rdfs:label "Weapon property definition"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A weapon property as the SRD 5.2.1 edition describes it, kept as the edition's prose. The record is data only: reading a property as a parameter or precondition of an attack is a separate, later interpretation and is not made by this record."@en .

#################################################################
# Weapon-definition and D20 concretions over kosmion/participatorium (weapon records are Descriptions as of the 2026-07-27 re-home)
#################################################################

## LINEAGE: NEW MINT with no predecessor, minted 2026-08-14; ruled by the product seat 2026-08-14
## (the currency-package seam's two-sided row vocabulary — a value equation has TWO sides, so the
## one-sided kosm:quantity + kosm:fungibleKind pair is refused ON THE ROW and carried by each side).
srd521:CurrencyEquation
  a cat:Kind ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Description ;
  rdfs:label "Currency equation"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "One row of the edition's Coin Values table, stated as a value equation between two denominated amounts: a coin side and a value side that are worth the same. The row itself bears no amount; each side is a currency equation side carrying exactly one quantity and one denomination."@en .

## LINEAGE: NEW MINT with no predecessor, minted 2026-08-14; ruled by the product seat 2026-08-14
## (the seam's side carrier: each side IS one denominated amount, hence the amount-bearer
## specialization the row class deliberately does not have).
srd521:CurrencyEquationSide
  a cat:Kind ;
  cat:specializes cat:AmountBearer ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Description ;
  rdfs:label "Currency equation side"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "One side of a currency equation: a single denominated amount, carried as one decimal quantity paired with one fungible-kind denomination."@en .

srd521:WeaponDefinition
  a cat:Kind ;
  cat:specializes cat:AmountBearer ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Description ;
  rdfs:label "Weapon definition"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "RE-HOMED to the SpellDefinition idiom (WT-3 ripple + SB-2, 2026-07-27; was a cat:SecondOrderType categorizing kosm:Item): a weapon record is a STATBLOCK — authored edition content, a cat:Description — not a kind of thing. The prior idiom asserted a rigid artifact-kind claim the source never makes, and it fell with kosm:Item's demotion. Kind-hood and item-type assertions belong in WORLD content (kosm:ItemType), where a world that stocks battleaxes says so; the rules package holds the statblock only."@en .
## Joined cat:AmountBearer directly on 2026-08-11; ruled by the product seat 2026-08-11. The cat:Kind
## metatype and cat:Description instance category are unchanged.

srd521:D20Test
  a cat:EventType ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Action ;
  rdfs:label "D20 test"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The base edition action event-type for uncertain tests resolved by a D20 procedure."@en .

srd521:D20TestType
  a cat:SecondOrderType ;
  cat:specializes par:ActionType ;
  cat:categorizes srd521:D20Test ;
  rdfs:label "D20 test type"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The edition category whose members are D20 test action-types such as ability check, saving throw, and attack roll."@en .

srd521:D20TestWarrant
  a cat:Kind ;
  cat:specializes par:Warrant ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Relator ;
  rdfs:label "D20 test warrant"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "An edition warrant requesting resolution by a D20 test. It uses participatorium's three-way Warrant mediation and resolution-parameter machinery."@en .

srd521:D20TestWarrantWithdrawal
  a cat:EventType ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Event ;
  rdfs:label "D20 test warrant withdrawal"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "An event that withdraws an open D20 test warrant through par:withdrawsWarrant."@en .

srd521:D20TestWarrantDecline
  a cat:EventType ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Event ;
  rdfs:label "D20 test warrant decline"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "An event that declines an open D20 test warrant through par:declinesWarrant."@en .

srd521:D20RollProcedure
  a cat:Description ;
  cat:instanceOf par:RollProcedure ;
  rdfs:label "D20 roll procedure"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Roll 1d20, apply the relevant ability modifier, proficiency if applicable, and circumstantial modifiers, then compare the total with the warranted target number."@en .

srd521:D20RollEvidence
  a cat:Kind ;
  cat:specializes par:RollEvidence ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:InformationObject ;
  rdfs:label "D20 roll evidence"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The committed evidence record of one roll in the edition's D20 family: an attack roll, ability check, or saving throw. It holds the dice expression, the raw faces rolled, each modifier with its source, the total, and how the roll was produced. It records the roll only; whether the roll succeeded is decided in a separate outcome record, never here."@en .

srd521:D20RollModifier
  a cat:Kind ;
  cat:specializes par:ResolutionParameter ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Parameter ;
  rdfs:label "D20 roll modifier"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "One modifier contributing to a D20 roll's total, carried by that roll's evidence record: a signed whole number, the source it comes from, and its kind, such as an ability modifier, a proficiency bonus, or a circumstance bonus."@en .

srd521:DifficultyClass
  a cat:Kind ;
  cat:specializes par:ResolutionParameter ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Parameter ;
  rdfs:label "Difficulty Class"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A D20 resolution parameter whose numeric value is carried by par:targetNumber."@en .

srd521:D20TestOutcome
  a cat:SituationType ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Situation ;
  rdfs:label "D20 test outcome"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The base situation-type for adjudicated D20 test outcomes."@en .

srd521:D20OutcomeTier
  a cat:SecondOrderType ;
  cat:specializes par:OutcomeTier ;
  cat:partitions srd521:D20TestOutcome ;
  rdfs:label "D20 outcome tier"@en .

srd521:D20Success
  a cat:SituationType ;
  cat:instanceOf srd521:D20OutcomeTier, par:OutcomeTier ;
  cat:specializes srd521:D20TestOutcome ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Situation ;
  rdfs:label "D20 success"@en .

srd521:D20Failure
  a cat:SituationType ;
  cat:instanceOf srd521:D20OutcomeTier, par:OutcomeTier ;
  cat:specializes srd521:D20TestOutcome ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Situation ;
  rdfs:label "D20 failure"@en .

srd521:D20TestConsequence
  a cat:Kind ;
  cat:specializes par:ConsequenceTemplate ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Description ;
  rdfs:label "D20 test consequence"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A consequence that follows from an adjudicated D20 test, citing the outcome it follows from. Changes of state and withdrawals of actions are attached here or downstream of here; they are never made by rewriting the warrant that called for the test, the roll evidence, or the outcome record."@en .

#################################################################
# Edition action-types
#################################################################

srd521:Attack
  a cat:EventType ;
  cat:instanceOf par:ActionType ;
  cat:specializes par:Attack ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Action ;
  par:actionFacet par:manipulation ;
  cat:lexicalToken "attack" ;
  rdfs:label "Attack"@en .

srd521:Dash
  a cat:EventType ;
  cat:instanceOf par:ActionType ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Action ;
  par:actionFacet par:relocation ;
  cat:lexicalToken "dash" ;
  rdfs:label "Dash"@en .

srd521:Disengage
  a cat:EventType ;
  cat:instanceOf par:ActionType ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Action ;
  par:actionFacet par:relocation, par:selfState ;
  cat:lexicalToken "disengage" ;
  rdfs:label "Disengage"@en .

srd521:Dodge
  a cat:EventType ;
  cat:instanceOf par:ActionType ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Action ;
  par:actionFacet par:selfState ;
  cat:lexicalToken "dodge" ;
  rdfs:label "Dodge"@en .

srd521:Help
  a cat:EventType ;
  cat:instanceOf par:ActionType ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Action ;
  cat:lexicalToken "help" ;
  rdfs:label "Help"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A polymorphic edition action. It deliberately does NOT specialize par:Assist: Help covers several intentions (aiding a check, aiding an attack, and edition uses beyond assistance), so a type edge would over-claim — co-classification is per TOKEN, which is what par:Assist's own comment prescribes (\"D&D Help TOKENS that aid a check/attack co-classify, but Help-as-first-aid does NOT\"). ⛔ CORRECTED 2026-08-01: this comment previously gave the reason as \"par:Assist, whose intension is first aid,\" which inverts that term's landed text — first aid is the use par:Assist EXCLUDES, not its intension. Has no invariant facet profile, matching par:Assist's own no-fixed-facet stance."@en .

srd521:Hide
  a cat:EventType ;
  cat:instanceOf par:ActionType ;
  cat:specializes par:Hide ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Action ;
  par:actionFacet par:selfState ;
  cat:lexicalToken "hide" ;
  rdfs:label "Hide"@en .

srd521:Influence
  a cat:EventType ;
  cat:instanceOf par:ActionType ;
  cat:specializes par:Influence ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Action ;
  par:actionFacet par:communication ;
  cat:lexicalToken "influence" ;
  rdfs:label "Influence"@en .

srd521:Ready
  a cat:EventType ;
  cat:instanceOf par:ActionType ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Action ;
  par:actionFacet par:temporalFlow ;
  cat:lexicalToken "ready" ;
  rdfs:label "Ready"@en .

srd521:Search
  a cat:EventType ;
  cat:instanceOf par:ActionType ;
  cat:specializes par:Observe ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Action ;
  par:actionFacet par:perception ;
  cat:lexicalToken "search" ;
  rdfs:label "Search"@en .

srd521:Study
  a cat:EventType ;
  cat:instanceOf par:ActionType ;
  cat:specializes par:Investigate ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Action ;
  par:actionFacet par:cognition ;
  cat:lexicalToken "study" ;
  rdfs:label "Study"@en .

srd521:Utilize
  a cat:EventType ;
  cat:instanceOf par:ActionType ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Action ;
  par:actionFacet par:manipulation ;
  cat:lexicalToken "utilize" ;
  rdfs:label "Utilize"@en .

srd521:Cast
  a cat:EventType ;
  cat:instanceOf par:ActionType ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Action ;
  cat:lexicalToken "magic" ;
  rdfs:label "Magic"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The edition's spellcasting mechanism dispatcher. It has no common-catalog parent and no fixed facet profile; each spellcasting action token co-classifies to its real intention, such as par:Attack, par:Influence, or par:Observe."@en .

srd521:Attune
  a cat:EventType ;
  cat:instanceOf par:ActionType ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Action ;
  cat:lexicalToken "attune" ;
  rdfs:label "Attune"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The edition action that creates or maintains a D&D magic-item attunement. The bond relator machinery is kosm:Attunement; edition limits and slots remain srd521 content."@en .

#################################################################
# Attunement rules referencing kosmion's relator machinery
#################################################################

srd521:AttunementRule
  a cat:Kind ;
  cat:specializes par:DecisionRule ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Description ;
  rdfs:label "Attunement rule"@en .

srd521:AttunementLimit
  a cat:Kind ;
  cat:specializes par:ResolutionParameter ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Parameter ;
  rdfs:label "Attunement limit"@en .

srd521:AttunementSlot
  a cat:Kind ;
  cat:specializes par:ResolutionParameter ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Parameter ;
  rdfs:label "Attunement slot"@en .

srd521:attunementRelator
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:rangeType kosm:Attunement ;
  rdfs:label "attunement relator"@en .

srd521:attunementLimit
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:AttunementRule ;
  cat:rangeType srd521:AttunementLimit ;
  rdfs:label "attunement limit"@en .

srd521:attunementSlot
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType kosm:Attunement ;
  cat:rangeType srd521:AttunementSlot ;
  rdfs:label "attunement slot"@en .

#################################################################
# Edition-owned damage effect family
#################################################################

srd521:DamageEffect
  a cat:Kind ;
  cat:specializes par:ConsequenceTemplate ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Description ;
  rdfs:label "Damage effect"@en .

srd521:DamageEvidenceMode
  a cat:Kind ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Individual ;
  rdfs:label "Damage evidence mode"@en .

srd521:damageEvidenceMode_damageRoll
  a cat:Individual ;
  cat:instanceOf srd521:DamageEvidenceMode ;
  rdfs:label "damage roll"@en ;
  cat:lexicalToken "damage-roll" .

srd521:damageEvidenceMode_staticDamage
  a cat:Individual ;
  cat:instanceOf srd521:DamageEvidenceMode ;
  rdfs:label "static damage"@en ;
  cat:lexicalToken "static-damage" .

srd521:damageAmount
  a rdf:Property ;
  rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
  rdfs:label "damage amount"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The damage magnitude on damage evidence and committed condition effects (measured: battle-beat-attack.ts:301 on AttackDamageEvidence, :356 on ConditionEffect — domain deliberately undeclared for that reason). Absorbs the retiring dynamis-subroot dyn:damageAmount (declared 2026-07-31, declare-the-36; edition boundary per participatorium.ttl:583-587)."@en .

srd521:damageEvidenceMode
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:rangeType srd521:DamageEvidenceMode ;
  rdfs:label "damage evidence mode"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "How this damage evidence was produced. The platform currently writes the lexical token as a string literal (battle-beat-attack.ts:302); migration lifts literals to members via cat:lexicalToken. Absorbs the retiring dynamis-subroot dyn:damageEvidenceMode (declared 2026-07-31, declare-the-36; the destination kind and members pre-existed this session and already follow the member-prefix convention)."@en .

#################################################################
# Nine-fold alignment declaration terms
#################################################################

## SPECIALIZES rol:ValueSchemeTerm 2026-08-16 (CARD AV (e), Dave 2026-08-15; the edge lands with
##   the scheme mint): the family reaches theory through the TERM-FAMILY supertype, never through
##   rol:ValueScheme itself — a term family is not a scheme, and specializing the scheme would make
##   every alignment term a scheme instance.
srd521:AlignmentTerm
  a cat:Kind ;
  cat:specializes rol:ValueSchemeTerm ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Individual ;
  rdfs:label "Alignment term"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The edition family of declaration terms usable as rol:declarationTerm values on rol:ValueDeclaration records (rol:AlignmentDeclaration RETIRED 2026-08-15 with no successor: rol:ValueDeclaration absorbs it, and the alignment-vs-free-form discriminator is readable off the term rather than restated on the record). The family is governed by srd521:alignmentScheme, this edition's rol:ValueScheme: nine members sit on its two-axis grid and carry one rol:valueAxisPosition per axis; srd521:unaligned sits off the grid and is classified srd521:OffAxisAlignmentTerm instead."@en ;
  rdfs:seeAlso srd521:alignmentScheme, rol:ValueScheme, rol:ValueDeclaration, rol:declarationTerm,
    rol:ValueAxis, rol:ValueAxisPosition, rol:valueAxis, rol:valueAxisPosition .

srd521:lawfulGood
  a cat:Individual ;
  cat:instanceOf srd521:AlignmentTerm ;
  rol:valueAxisPosition srd521:valueAxisPosition_ethicsLawful, srd521:valueAxisPosition_moralsGood ;
  rdfs:label "Lawful Good"@en .

srd521:neutralGood
  a cat:Individual ;
  cat:instanceOf srd521:AlignmentTerm ;
  rol:valueAxisPosition srd521:valueAxisPosition_ethicsNeutral, srd521:valueAxisPosition_moralsGood ;
  rdfs:label "Neutral Good"@en .

srd521:chaoticGood
  a cat:Individual ;
  cat:instanceOf srd521:AlignmentTerm ;
  rol:valueAxisPosition srd521:valueAxisPosition_ethicsChaotic, srd521:valueAxisPosition_moralsGood ;
  rdfs:label "Chaotic Good"@en .

srd521:lawfulNeutral
  a cat:Individual ;
  cat:instanceOf srd521:AlignmentTerm ;
  rol:valueAxisPosition srd521:valueAxisPosition_ethicsLawful, srd521:valueAxisPosition_moralsNeutral ;
  rdfs:label "Lawful Neutral"@en .

srd521:neutral
  a cat:Individual ;
  cat:instanceOf srd521:AlignmentTerm ;
  rol:valueAxisPosition srd521:valueAxisPosition_ethicsNeutral, srd521:valueAxisPosition_moralsNeutral ;
  rdfs:label "Neutral"@en .

srd521:chaoticNeutral
