## RETIRED 2026-08-10 — srd521:rollEvidence. Dave ruled the cut in the product channel: an edition-typed
## clone of a general relation, whose narrowing is carried by SHACL, not by a second property.
## Absorbed by par:citesRollEvidence, which the frozen mapping row for the pre-family
## dynamis spelling now targets (class-3 freeze amendment, same act).
## MEASURED AT THE CUT: 0 authored carriers and 0 platform consumers at this IRI — the platform
## builds the dynamis spelling (packages/rules/src/index.ts:108 over dynamisVocab), so the
## "serves the landed consumers" rationale in the retired comment was never true of THIS term.
## The D20 typing it carried is already enforced at dyn-sh:D20TestOutcomeShape
## (ontology/modules/dynamis-shacl.ttl:964-969: path, minCount 1, maxCount 1, class).
## Reverses the DF-RESTORE-2 restoration (Dave, 2026-07-28) on new evidence, not as a tidy-up.


srd521:weaponDefinition
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType kosm:Item ;
  cat:rangeType srd521:WeaponDefinition ;
  rdfs:label "weapon definition"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Links one identity-bearing live item to its reusable rules-package weapon definition. Action options remain rules data and are derived by joining the item-action-option records; they are never copied onto the live item. RESTORED under DF-RESTORE-1 (Dave, 2026-07-28: 'a frozen row can be corrected') from pre-family possessio:weaponDefinition, whose comment this preserves. The frozen v2 row CASE-FOLDED this owl:ObjectProperty onto its class sibling srd521:WeaponDefinition, so the property was never minted while packages/contracts/src/terms.ts:131 kept exporting its IRI as campaignSeedWeaponDefinitionPredicate. Homed in srd521 rather than the family because its range is edition content; the frozen row already named this base and only the case was wrong."@en .

srd521:grantWeaponDefinition
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType kosm:ContentGrant ;
  cat:rangeType srd521:WeaponDefinition ;
  rdfs:label "grant weapon definition"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Links a content grant to the reusable rules-package weapon definition its granted item instantiates at founding. Minted 2026-08-05 (wave-1 slate-1 re-dispose, Dave in-channel). Homed by this file's own cross-base property pattern (cat:domainType kosm:Item at srd521:weaponDefinition, kosm:Attunement at srd521:AttunementRule, par:DecisionTable): an edition-specific relation whose meaning is the edition's - the granted item instantiates a 5.2.1 weapon definition. Absorbs the retiring sc:grantWeaponDefinition, which was never declared - used only as a SHACL path in the seed-founding contract (consult-2 finding 4 repairs this comment's first-landed provenance wording)."@en .

srd521:usesSkill
