## minted 2026-08-14, ruled by Dave (product channel: "yes, let's do that!"); NO PREDECESSOR.
## Ground: design-by-use — the character-sheet contract's required hit-die slot and the ruled
## POC character generator read this per class. Data rides the regeneration pipeline (the class
## rows do not carry it yet; the four non-caster classes land with the same regeneration).
srd521:classHitDie
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:CharacterClass ;
  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:label "class hit die"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The die a character of this class gains per level - the per-level hit-die entitlement, written as a die token such as \"d10\", as the source class table states it. Distinct from srd521:hitDiceExpression, which is a creature statline's hit-point generation expression, not a per-level entitlement."@en .

## RETIRED 2026-08-12 — srd521:costText. Dave ruled the retirement in the product channel
## (2026-08-12 00:18 PDT): "yes, let's retire costText. Seems like a source of drift and confusion."
## The drift is the term's own shape — one printed price held as an unparsed string beside the same
## price held normalized, two spellings of a single fact with nothing reconciling them.
## SUCCEEDED BY the normalized pair kosm:quantity + kosm:fungibleKind on the same WeaponDefinition,
## which the retired declaration's carrier comment anticipated and which the extraction generator now
## emits (stagecraft 019a2005) — landed in weapons/weapons.ttl by THIS commit. The declaration's
## removal rides the regeneration's own epoch and never precedes it, so no window exists in which the
## landed values are used-but-undeclared.
## THE BYTE-FAITHFUL SOURCE IS UNCHANGED: weapons/weapons.csv carries the printed cost string verbatim
## and remains the extraction evidence this property was minted to hold. The retirement drops the
## derived second copy, not the source, so no fidelity is lost.
## MEASURED AT THE CUT (at the files, this commit): weapons.ttl costText 38 -> 0, kosm:quantity 0 -> 38,
## kosm:fungibleKind 0 -> 38 (CP 1, SP 5, GP 32), 1174 -> 1212 triples, weaponWeight byte-identical by
## hash. Zero behavioural consumers at this IRI (census over 2,440 files / 17 repos); the surviving
## occurrence records are stagecraft's term inventory and resolution map, which regenerate at the srd
## pin roll and are deliberately not touched here.

srd521:weaponWeight
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:WeaponDefinition ;
  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:label "weapon weight"@en .

srd521:sourceProperties
  a rdf:Property ;
  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:label "source properties"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The properties column of a weapon's row in the edition's table, preserved as the text printed there rather than parsed into structured property records."@en .

srd521:damageExpression
  a rdf:Property ;
  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:label "damage expression"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Damage stated as a dice expression, for damage data taken from the edition. Non-empty values use the same compact dice notation as roll evidence; damage the edition states as a fixed number is recorded with srd521:staticDamage instead."@en .

srd521:staticDamage
