#################################################################
## §SW-7 COMBAT RECORDS (RULED 2026-07-25 — the edition arm)
## The census flagged these as records "Lane A deliberately did NOT invent". They land HERE, not in
## participatorium, on the standing general-vs-edition charter line: participatorium owns the
## GENERAL organized-play machinery (par:Intent, par:RollEvidence, par:Attack as an ActionType,
## par:Encounter and par:EncounterEngagement — the last RULED general by Dave the same day), and
## srd521 owns what is 5.2.1-specific: the attack/damage EVIDENCE shapes and encounter posture.
## Every term below cat:specializes its participatorium general, so a second edition mints its own
## records without either vocabulary learning about the other.
#################################################################

srd521:AttackIntent a cat:Kind ;
  cat:specializes par:Intent ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:InformationObject ;
  rdfs:label "Attack intent"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A declared intent to attack, in 5.2.1 terms — the artifact a warrant adjudicates. Specializes the general par:Intent; edition-specific because the parameters it carries (attack mode, roll kind, item) are this edition's." .

## RETIRED 2026-08-06 — srd521:attackActor WITHDRAWN, no successor minted here: it re-expresses onto
## par:intentForActant (Dave 2026-08-06). The two were the same relation and the edition one
## stated no meaning of its own — identical cat:rangeType kosm:Actant, and its cat:domainType
## srd521:AttackIntent cat:specializes par:Intent, which is par:intentForActant's own domain,
## so every AttackIntent already qualifies. It carried NO rdfs:comment because there was no
## distinct thing to say; its mapping rule was round2-minted-same-local, generated rather than
## argued. A shape targeting srd521:AttackIntent constrains par:intentForActant on that focus
## node without a separate predicate. Contrast its pair srd521:attackOpponent, which states a
## reasoned naming decision and stays: the family has no "the one attacked" relation.
## Frozen mapping RETARGETS the row (srd521 -> par) by freeze amendment in the same act — a
## base change, so binding rule 3 does NOT cover it.

srd521:attackOpponent a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:AttackIntent ; cat:rangeType kosm:Actant ;
  rdfs:label "attack opponent"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The declared target. NOT named attackTarget — target is overloaded across the estate (consequence targets, state targets, desire targets); opponent is unambiguous in an attack." .

srd521:attackItem a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:AttackIntent ; rdfs:range cat:Object ;
  rdfs:label "attack item"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The weapon or object used. Range is cat:Object rather than kosm:Item per W-2 — an improvised rock is not an Item but attacks with it are legal." .

srd521:AttackRollEvidence a cat:Kind ;
  cat:specializes par:RollEvidence ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:InformationObject ;
  rdfs:label "Attack roll evidence"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The immutable record produced by an attack roll event. Specializes par:RollEvidence and inherits its law: produced by the event via information-flow (never causation), immutable once committed." .

srd521:AttackDamageEvidence a cat:Kind ;
  cat:specializes par:ResolutionEvidence ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:InformationObject ;
  rdfs:label "Attack damage evidence"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The immutable record of damage dealt. Kept SEPARATE from AttackRollEvidence because the two are produced by different events and either can exist without the other — automatic-hit damage has no attack roll, and a missed attack has a roll with no damage. Carries the existing srd521:damageAmount / damageType / damageExpression vocabulary. RE-PARENTED par:RollEvidence → par:ResolutionEvidence 2026-07-31 (court ④(a), close-review F10): a static-damage record (contracts/battle-beat.ts:108) is produced by NO roll, which falsified the RollEvidence parent against that class's own produced-by-the-roll-event definition." .

srd521:forAttackIntent a rdf:Property ;
  cat:rangeType srd521:AttackIntent ;
  rdfs:label "for attack intent"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Evidence record → the intent it answers. Domain deliberately open: both evidence kinds use it." .

srd521:adjudicatesDamageEvidence a rdf:Property ;
  cat:rangeType srd521:AttackDamageEvidence ;
  rdfs:label "adjudicates damage evidence"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The adjudication act → the damage evidence it rules on. Kept on the ADJUDICATING side, consistent with the ruled token-on-the-event-side discipline (participatorium R3)." .

srd521:EncounterPostureKind a cat:Kind ;
  rdfs:label "Encounter posture kind"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Enum: members are cat:instanceOf it (no punning). A combatant's posture within an encounter. ⚠️ FALSE-FRIEND GUARD: this is the home of the retiring bare sc:standing — which is ENCOUNTER POSTURE and must NEVER map to psy:persistenceKind_standing (renamed from psy:standing 2026-08-14, which dissolves the near-name) (psychikon's SOCIAL standing, an entirely different concept). The census flagged this pair explicitly." .

srd521:standingPosture cat:instanceOf srd521:EncounterPostureKind ; rdfs:label "standing"@en .
srd521:pronePosture    cat:instanceOf srd521:EncounterPostureKind ; rdfs:label "prone"@en .

srd521:encounterPosture a rdf:Property ;
  cat:rangeType srd521:EncounterPostureKind ;
  rdfs:label "encounter posture"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A combatant to its posture. Deliberately NOT named 'standing' — the bare local name is the psy:persistenceKind_standing (renamed from psy:standing 2026-08-14, which dissolves the near-name) false friend, and naming the property for the axis rather than one of its values makes the collision unspellable." .

#################################################################
## §SB-1 STATBLOCKS (product desk 2026-07-25 — the creature arm; design: flag.task.2026-07-25_2200-statblock-package)
## The fifth statblock package: creatures. srd521:CreatureDefinition mirrors the WeaponDefinition charter
## shape over kosmion's reserved seam (kosm:CreatureType's own comment: "srd521 statblock species
## are cat:instanceOf it"). Statblock scalars follow the flat weapons idiom: per-statblock speed and
## sense-range properties rather than qualified entries. Skill proficiencies are the exception and
## get qualified CreatureSkillProficiency rows because printed skill bonuses are NOT derivable
## (expertise: the SRD Wolf's Perception +5 = WIS +1 plus twice PB +2). REUSED, not redeclared:
## saveAbility, damageExpression, damageType, sourceSection, usesSkill, the AlignmentTerm
## individuals, and the abilities/ skills/ damage-types/ conditions/ packages. The item-side
## attackMode and normalRangeFeet/longRangeFeet are cat:domainType-locked to ItemActionOption, so
## the creature arm carries its own rangeNormalFeet/rangeLongFeet and leaves attack mode to the
## verbatim actionText.
#################################################################

srd521:CreatureDefinition
  a cat:Kind ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Description ;
  rdfs:label "Creature definition"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "RE-HOMED to the SpellDefinition idiom (SB-2 ruled + WT-3, 2026-07-27; was a cat:SecondOrderType whose own comment mandated 'the statblock is the KIND'): a creature record is a STATBLOCK — authored edition content, a cat:Description — and the statblock-is-the-kind mandate was the term conflating 'statistical template' with 'kind of thing' (two independent derivations found the same defect: the cat:Kind over-commitment on occupations, and CreatureDefinition's inability to hold a foreign statline). Species-hood lives in WORLD content — 'wolves are a species' is a kosm:CreatureType assertion where it was always true; an occupation statblock (bandit, guard) asserts no species at all; a named NPC is a kosmion actant whose world classification references its statblock by cat:describedBy."@en .

srd521:CreatureActionOption
  a cat:Kind ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Description ;
  rdfs:label "Creature action option"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A trait, action, bonus-action, reaction, or legendary-action row of a statblock. The verbatim SRD prose is srd521:actionText; structured attack/save/damage fields are added only where the statblock prints them, and pure-prose traits stay prose rows."@en .

srd521:CreatureSkillProficiency
  a cat:Kind ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Description ;
  rdfs:label "Creature skill proficiency"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A qualified skill-proficiency row (creature, skill, printed bonus). Qualified rather than a bare reference because the SRD prints per-skill bonuses that are not derivable from ability and CR alone."@en .

srd521:SizeKind
  a cat:Kind ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Individual ;
  rdfs:label "Size kind"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Enum: members are cat:instanceOf it (no punning). The six SRD 5.2.1 creature size categories; members live in sizes/."@en .

srd521:CreatureTypeKind
  a cat:Kind ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Individual ;
  rdfs:label "Creature type kind"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Enum: members are cat:instanceOf it (no punning). The fourteen SRD 5.2.1 creature types; members live in creature-types/."@en .

srd521:SenseKind
  a cat:Kind ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Individual ;
  rdfs:label "Sense kind"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Enum: members are cat:instanceOf it (no punning). The SRD 5.2.1 special senses; members live in sense-kinds/. Creature statblocks carry flat per-record ranges (darkvisionFeet etc.); the enum records the vocabulary."@en .

srd521:SpeedKind
  a cat:Kind ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Individual ;
  rdfs:label "Speed kind"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Enum: members are cat:instanceOf it (no punning). The SRD 5.2.1 movement kinds; members live in speed-kinds/. Creature statblocks carry flat per-record speeds (walkSpeedFeet etc.); the enum records the vocabulary."@en .

srd521:CreatureActionKind
  a cat:Kind ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Individual ;
  rdfs:label "Creature action kind"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Enum: members are cat:instanceOf it (no punning). The statblock section a CreatureActionOption row belongs to. Members are declared inline here (the DamageEvidenceMode precedent) because they are statblock structure, not glossary vocabulary."@en .

srd521:actionKind_trait
  a cat:Individual ;
  cat:instanceOf srd521:CreatureActionKind ;
  rdfs:label "trait"@en .

srd521:actionKind_action
  a cat:Individual ;
  cat:instanceOf srd521:CreatureActionKind ;
  rdfs:label "action"@en .

srd521:actionKind_bonusAction
  a cat:Individual ;
  cat:instanceOf srd521:CreatureActionKind ;
  rdfs:label "bonus action"@en .

srd521:actionKind_reaction
  a cat:Individual ;
  cat:instanceOf srd521:CreatureActionKind ;
  rdfs:label "reaction"@en .

srd521:actionKind_legendaryAction
  a cat:Individual ;
  cat:instanceOf srd521:CreatureActionKind ;
  rdfs:label "legendary action"@en .

## Absorbs no predecessor; the OffAxisAlignmentTerm membership is added 2026-08-11, ruled by Dave
##   2026-08-11 (product channel). It KEEPS srd521:AlignmentTerm: srd521:alignment's cat:rangeType is
##   AlignmentTerm, so dropping that membership would invalidate every statblock using this term
##   (the SRD Wolf at creatures/creatures.ttl). The off-axis classification is additive, never a move.
srd521:unaligned
  a cat:Individual ;
  cat:instanceOf srd521:AlignmentTerm, srd521:OffAxisAlignmentTerm ;
  rdfs:label "Unaligned"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The statblock alignment of creatures that lack moral agency (the SRD Wolf is Unaligned). Extends the nine-fold family for statblock use; 'Character Creation' describes the nine alignments and unaligned creatures. It sits off the two-axis grid rather than at a cell of it, and so occupies no position on either axis."@en .

srd521:armorClass
  a rdf:Property ;
  rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
  rdfs:label "armor class"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Domain deliberately open: the PC/creature shared core (abilities, AC, HP) converges on these terms."@en .

srd521:armorClassText
  a rdf:Property ;
  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:label "armor class text"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The source's AC parenthetical, when one is printed. Domain deliberately open, paired with armorClass."@en .

srd521:hitPointsAverage
  a rdf:Property ;
  rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
  rdfs:label "hit points average"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The printed Hit Points number. Domain deliberately open (shared core)."@en .

srd521:hitDiceExpression
  a rdf:Property ;
  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:label "hit dice expression"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The printed Hit Point Dice parenthetical, e.g. '2d8 + 2'. Domain deliberately open (shared core)."@en .

srd521:strengthScore
  a rdf:Property ;
  rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
  rdfs:label "Strength score"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Ability scores are flat integer properties (the flat weapons idiom); the abilities dataset remains the vocabulary anchor. Domain deliberately open (shared core)."@en .

srd521:dexterityScore
  a rdf:Property ;
  rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
  rdfs:label "Dexterity score"@en .

srd521:constitutionScore
  a rdf:Property ;
  rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
  rdfs:label "Constitution score"@en .

srd521:intelligenceScore
  a rdf:Property ;
  rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
  rdfs:label "Intelligence score"@en .

srd521:wisdomScore
  a rdf:Property ;
  rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
  rdfs:label "Wisdom score"@en .

srd521:charismaScore
  a rdf:Property ;
  rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
  rdfs:label "Charisma score"@en .

srd521:sizeKind
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:CreatureDefinition ;
  cat:rangeType srd521:SizeKind ;
  rdfs:label "size kind"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Multi-valued when the statblock offers size options, e.g. 'Medium or Small Humanoid'."@en .

srd521:creatureTypeKind
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:CreatureDefinition ;
  cat:rangeType srd521:CreatureTypeKind ;
  rdfs:label "creature type kind"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Multi-valued for multi-type statblocks, e.g. 'Large Celestial, Fey, or Fiend'."@en .

srd521:alignment
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:CreatureDefinition ;
  cat:rangeType srd521:AlignmentTerm ;
  rdfs:label "alignment"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The statblock's default alignment suggestion, definition-level. Individual actants declare theirs via rol:ValueDeclaration, whose term is an srd521:AlignmentTerm."@en .

srd521:challengeRating
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:CreatureDefinition ;
  rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
  rdfs:label "challenge rating"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Fractional CRs are decimals: CR 1/8 = 0.125, CR 1/4 = 0.25."@en .

srd521:xpValue
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:CreatureDefinition ;
  rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
  rdfs:label "XP value"@en .

srd521:proficiencyBonus
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:CreatureDefinition ;
  rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
  rdfs:label "proficiency bonus"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Printed in the statblock's CR line ('CR 1/8 (XP 25; PB +2)'); recorded so the line is lossless."@en .

srd521:walkSpeedFeet
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:CreatureDefinition ;
  rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
  rdfs:label "walk speed in feet"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Per-statblock flat speed properties (the flat weapons idiom) rather than qualified speed entries; speed-kinds/ records the vocabulary."@en .

srd521:flySpeedFeet
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:CreatureDefinition ;
  rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
  rdfs:label "fly speed in feet"@en .

srd521:swimSpeedFeet
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:CreatureDefinition ;
  rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
  rdfs:label "swim speed in feet"@en .

srd521:burrowSpeedFeet
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:CreatureDefinition ;
  rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
  rdfs:label "burrow speed in feet"@en .

srd521:climbSpeedFeet
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:CreatureDefinition ;
  rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
  rdfs:label "climb speed in feet"@en .

srd521:canHover
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:CreatureDefinition ;
  rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
  rdfs:label "can hover"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "True when the statblock's Fly Speed carries the '(hover)' qualifier, e.g. 'Fly 20 ft. (hover)'."@en .

srd521:darkvisionFeet
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:CreatureDefinition ;
  rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
  rdfs:label "darkvision range in feet"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Per-statblock flat sense-range properties (the flat weapons idiom) rather than qualified sense entries; sense-kinds/ records the vocabulary."@en .

srd521:blindsightFeet
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:CreatureDefinition ;
  rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
  rdfs:label "blindsight range in feet"@en .

srd521:tremorsenseFeet
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:CreatureDefinition ;
  rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
  rdfs:label "tremorsense range in feet"@en .

srd521:truesightFeet
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:CreatureDefinition ;
  rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
  rdfs:label "truesight range in feet"@en .

srd521:passivePerception
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:CreatureDefinition ;
  rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
  rdfs:label "passive Perception"@en .

srd521:saveProficiency
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:CreatureDefinition ;
  cat:rangeType srd521:AbilityScore ;
  rdfs:label "save proficiency"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Marks an ability whose statblock SAVE entry exceeds its MOD entry; the printed save bonus is mod plus PB."@en .

srd521:skillBonus
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:CreatureSkillProficiency ;
  rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
  rdfs:label "skill bonus"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The printed per-skill bonus, e.g. 'Stealth +4' records 4."@en .

srd521:resistsDamageType
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:CreatureDefinition ;
  cat:rangeType srd521:DamageType ;
  rdfs:label "resists damage type"@en .

srd521:immuneToDamageType
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:CreatureDefinition ;
  cat:rangeType srd521:DamageType ;
  rdfs:label "immune to damage type"@en .

srd521:vulnerableToDamageType
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:CreatureDefinition ;
  cat:rangeType srd521:DamageType ;
  rdfs:label "vulnerable to damage type"@en .

srd521:immuneToCondition
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:CreatureDefinition ;
  cat:rangeType srd521:ConditionDefinition ;
  rdfs:label "immune to condition"@en .

srd521:languagesText
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:CreatureDefinition ;
  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:label "languages text"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The statblock's Languages line, verbatim ('None' stays 'None')."@en .

srd521:forCreature
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:rangeType srd521:CreatureDefinition ;
  rdfs:label "for creature"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A row to its creature statblock (a CreatureDefinition Description). Domain deliberately open: CreatureActionOption and CreatureSkillProficiency rows both use it (the forItem precedent, generalized)."@en .

srd521:actionKind
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:CreatureActionOption ;
  cat:rangeType srd521:CreatureActionKind ;
  rdfs:label "action kind"@en .

srd521:attackBonus
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:CreatureActionOption ;
  rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
  rdfs:label "attack bonus"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The printed attack-roll modifier: 'Melee Attack Roll: +4' records 4."@en .

srd521:reachFeet
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:CreatureActionOption ;
  rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
  rdfs:label "reach in feet"@en .

srd521:rangeNormalFeet
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:CreatureActionOption ;
  rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
  rdfs:label "normal range in feet (creature action)"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Creature-side twin of normalRangeFeet, which is cat:domainType-locked to ItemActionOption. Spelled range-first to keep the pair adjacent; harmonizing the two pairs is a desk call, flagged in the SB-1 build report."@en .

srd521:rangeLongFeet
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:CreatureActionOption ;
  rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
  rdfs:label "long range in feet (creature action)"@en .

srd521:saveDc
  a rdf:Property ;
  rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
  rdfs:label "save DC"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A printed fixed save DC. Domain deliberately open: statblock action rows and spellcasting prose both print fixed DCs."@en .

srd521:damageAverage
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:CreatureActionOption ;
  rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
  rdfs:label "damage average"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The printed average preceding the dice parenthetical: 'Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2)' records 5 with damageExpression '1d6 + 2' — the hitPointsAverage/hitDiceExpression pair idiom."@en .

srd521:rechargeText
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:CreatureActionOption ;
  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:label "recharge text"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The printed usage-limit qualifier, e.g. 'Recharge 5–6' or '3/Day'."@en .

srd521:actionText
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:CreatureActionOption ;
  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:label "action text"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The row's verbatim SRD prose."@en .

#################################################################
## §DECLARE-THE-36 — THE SRD SIX (RULED row-by-row, Dave + Francis, 2026-07-31)
## Rows: sc:StagedAttack · sc:commitsConditionEffect · dyn:damageAmount · dyn:damageEvidenceMode ·
## sc:rangeBand · sc:rangeRulesBasis. Two rows resolved to ALREADY-LANDED destinations
## (srd521:damageAmount, srd521:damageEvidenceMode — lineage sentences added in place); the rest
## are declared below. Court rulings applied: ④(a) — srd521:AttackDamageEvidence re-parented onto
## par:ResolutionEvidence (see its stanza); ⑤(c) — the rangeRulesBasis JSON blob DECOMPOSES and is
## never blessed (three of its seven fields were IRIs flattened into a literal at write time —
## battle-beat-attack.ts:182). Enum mints follow the ruled sflo member-prefix convention AND the
## file's own landed neighbor idiom (srd521:DamageEvidenceMode + damageEvidenceMode_* — natural-head
## class, prefixed members), which is the wave-2 endpoint; no *Kind suffix is minted to be renamed.
#################################################################

srd521:StagedAttack
  a cat:Kind ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:InformationObject ;
  rdfs:label "Staged attack"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "An attack record staged against a scene and awaiting resolution — pending-until-answered, the rol:ProposedCommitment logic (an unresolved staging mediates nothing yet). Edition-owned per the participatorium boundary (edition-specific attack/damage records are the edition package's — participatorium.ttl:583-587). Absorbs the retiring sc:StagedAttack (declared 2026-07-31, declare-the-36; fixture: inn-state:976-982, 'staged against the Inn scene and waits on branch-local continuity resolution'; its temporal-scope placement COMPOSES per the temporaenum §SW-7 decline of sc:stagedInTemporalScope, and its continuity debt rides tmpo:hasContinuityDebt)."@en .

srd521:commitsConditionEffect
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:rangeType srd521:ConditionEffect ;
  rdfs:label "commits condition effect"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "An attack-consequence adjudication to the srd521:ConditionEffect record it commits. Domain deliberately open: the platform writes it from BOTH the journal adjudication record AND the committed session event (battle-beat-attack.ts:373 and :381). Absorbs the retiring sc:commitsConditionEffect (declared 2026-07-31, declare-the-36)."@en .

srd521:RangeBand
  a cat:Kind ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Individual ;
  rdfs:label "Range band"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Enum (SF pattern; the srd521:DamageEvidenceMode idiom): the attack-time distance classification of an attack intent. NOT srd521:WeaponRangeKind (the weapon's two-way melee/ranged category); this is the classifier's six-way band over a measured distance. Closed by the executable contract (packages/rules/src/range-band.ts:13). Minted 2026-07-31, declare-the-36, backing the sc:rangeBand row."@en .

srd521:rangeBand_melee a cat:Individual ; cat:instanceOf srd521:RangeBand ; rdfs:label "Melee"@en ; cat:lexicalToken "melee" .
srd521:rangeBand_reach a cat:Individual ; cat:instanceOf srd521:RangeBand ; rdfs:label "Reach"@en ; cat:lexicalToken "reach" .
srd521:rangeBand_normal a cat:Individual ; cat:instanceOf srd521:RangeBand ; rdfs:label "Normal"@en ; cat:lexicalToken "normal" .
srd521:rangeBand_long a cat:Individual ; cat:instanceOf srd521:RangeBand ; rdfs:label "Long"@en ; cat:lexicalToken "long" .
srd521:rangeBand_outOfRange a cat:Individual ; cat:instanceOf srd521:RangeBand ; rdfs:label "Out of range"@en ; cat:lexicalToken "out-of-range" .
srd521:rangeBand_unknown a cat:Individual ; cat:instanceOf srd521:RangeBand ; rdfs:label "Unknown"@en ; cat:lexicalToken "unknown" ;
  rdfs:comment "The classifier's honest no-confident-band verdict ('never a confident band' — range-band.ts:129); WHY it is unknown stays code-side (DistanceUnknownKind) until a consumer needs it in RDF. Included per the psy:knowledgeStatusKind_notKnown honest-enum precedent."@en .

srd521:rangeBand
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:rangeType srd521:RangeBand ;
  rdfs:label "range band"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The classified distance band of an attack intent (measured subject: the platform's AttackIntent journal record — battle-beat-attack.ts:181; domain deliberately open for that reason). The platform currently writes the lexical token as a string literal; migration lifts literals to members via cat:lexicalToken. Absorbs the retiring sc:rangeBand (declared 2026-07-31, declare-the-36)."@en .

## ⑤(c): the basis record. The retiring sc:rangeRulesBasis carried JSON.stringify of a 7-field
## struct (range-band.ts:60-68) in which THREE fields were already IRIs. The blob is never blessed:
## these declarations ARE the decomposed target shape; the emission change rides the named re-IRI
## lane. Ruled ⑤(c), Dave, 2026-07-31.

srd521:RangeRulesBasis
  a cat:Kind ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:InformationObject ;
  rdfs:label "Range rules basis"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The computed citation record for one range-band classification: which rules and definitions grounded the band call. Committed evidence, immutable once written; minted per attack intent."@en .

srd521:rangeRulesBasis
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:rangeType srd521:RangeRulesBasis ;
  rdfs:label "range rules basis"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "An attack intent to its basis record. Absorbs the retiring sc:rangeRulesBasis, whose JSON-blob value DECOMPOSES into this record's fields at migration — the blob itself never receives a blessed IRI (⑤(c), declared 2026-07-31, declare-the-36)."@en .

srd521:basisActionRule
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:RangeRulesBasis ;
  rdfs:label "basis action rule"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The consulted weapon-action rule resource (measured: action?.iri, range-band.ts:265; the referent carries its own srd521:sourceSection). Range deliberately open until the action-row class is pinned by its own declaration."@en .

srd521:basisActionSourceSection
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:RangeRulesBasis ;
  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:label "basis action source section"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The SRD section label of the consulted action rule, CACHED at classification time — the referenced row's srd521:sourceSection as read then; evidence, not a live pointer."@en .

srd521:basisMeleeReachSource
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:RangeRulesBasis ;
  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:label "basis melee reach source"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Citation for the base melee reach applied (policy.baseMeleeReachSource, range-band.ts:266)."@en .

srd521:basisRangeProperty
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:RangeRulesBasis ;
  cat:rangeType srd521:WeaponPropertyDefinition ;
  rdfs:label "basis range property"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The weapon Range property definition consulted (measured: policy.rangePropertyDefinition.iri, range-band.ts:270 — a weapon-properties row, cat:instanceOf srd521:WeaponPropertyDefinition)."@en .

srd521:basisReachProperty
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:RangeRulesBasis ;
  cat:rangeType srd521:WeaponPropertyDefinition ;
  rdfs:label "basis reach property"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The weapon Reach property definition consulted, when the weapon has one (measured: reach?.iri, range-band.ts:271 — optional by construction)."@en .

srd521:basisNormalBoundary
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:RangeRulesBasis ;
  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:label "basis normal boundary"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Boundary posture applied at the weapon's normal range — closed value 'inclusive' (a distance exactly AT normal range classifies normal; range-band.ts:53). A verified policy reading, deliberately NOT an enum: it earns members only if the SRD ever offers a second posture (the named escalation trigger)."@en .

srd521:basisLongBoundary
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:RangeRulesBasis ;
  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:label "basis long boundary"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Boundary posture applied at the weapon's long range — closed value 'inclusive' (range-band.ts:54); same escalation trigger as basisNormalBoundary. The retiring blob FUSED these two policy fields into one 'normal-inclusive,long-inclusive' string; the decomposition follows the SOURCE structure (RangeBandPolicy), not the blob's."@en .

srd521:RollMode
  a cat:Kind ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:Individual ;
  rdfs:label "Roll mode"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Enum (SF pattern; the srd521:DamageEvidenceMode idiom): the D20 roll-mode dial — roll twice and take the higher (advantage) or the lower (disadvantage). Minted 2026-07-31 (declare-the-36) on the finding that the mechanic was VOCABULARY-HOMELESS: it existed only as TypeScript literal types, string literals in journal emissions (sc:submissionRollMode — intent.ts), JSON-blob fields, and rule-text prose. Future target for the sc:submissionRollMode disposition (flagged to the mapping); cat:lexicalToken is the lift bridge."@en .

srd521:rollMode_advantage
  a cat:Individual ;
  cat:instanceOf srd521:RollMode ;
  rdfs:label "Advantage"@en ;
  cat:lexicalToken "advantage" ;
  rdfs:comment "Roll twice, take the higher."@en .

srd521:rollMode_disadvantage
  a cat:Individual ;
  cat:instanceOf srd521:RollMode ;
  rdfs:label "Disadvantage"@en ;
  cat:lexicalToken "disadvantage" ;
  rdfs:comment "Roll twice, take the lower."@en .

srd521:basisLongRangeAttackRoll
  a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:RangeRulesBasis ;
  cat:rangeType srd521:RollMode ;
  rdfs:label "basis long range attack roll"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The roll-mode consequence READ OFF the cited Range rule for attacks beyond normal range — srd521:rollMode_disadvantage, regex-verified at policy construction (createSrdRangeBandPolicy REFUSES unless the referenced definition's own text matches 'beyond normal range…Disadvantage' — range-band.ts:86-89). An applied reading whose authority is the referenced definition; remodeled from the blob's string constant on Dave's smell (2026-07-31)."@en .

## WAVE-4 BATTLE-BEAT MINTS (Dave's batch word to planning 2026-08-05 20:34, on the slate as amended
## by the Cinderwash supersession - ruling record at planning's freeze; slate drop 2026-08-05-wave4-slate
## + -rows1-6-cinderwash. The retiring sc: terms split or retarget per those rows.)

srd521:AttackConsequenceAdjudication a cat:Kind ;
  cat:instanceCategory cat:InformationObject ;
  rdfs:label "Attack consequence adjudication"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The record of an authority's adjudication of an attack's consequences: it rules on the damage evidence before it (srd521:adjudicatesDamageEvidence, whose landed comment already names this act) and identifies what the consequences affect. Edition-scoped because what it adjudicates - this edition's attack intents, rolls and damage - is edition machinery; the general adjudication theory stays participatorium's by reference. Shape-only origin: sc:AttackConsequenceAdjudication was never declared - the battle-beat contract SHACL and evidence fixtures are its rung. Re-homed srd521: from the frozen row's par: target by the wave-4 batch ruling (2026-08-05, the amendment-#9 homing test: indistinguishable from its Attack* siblings without edition subject matter; the v3 retarget rides the next compose batch)." .

srd521:standing a rdf:Property ;
  cat:rangeType srd521:EncounterPostureKind ;
  rdfs:label "standing"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A combatant's posture within an encounter, as an EncounterPostureKind member. THE SITE SPLIT, ruled wave-4 2026-08-05: the retiring sc:standing converts here at POSTURE sites ONLY - at warrant sites its armed/fired/withdrawn values are the warrant relator's own lifecycle (created-unfired, fired, withdrawn termination) and dissolve into cat:createdIn/cat:terminatedIn on par:Warrant, never converting here - and psychikon's psy:persistenceKind_standing (renamed from psy:standing 2026-08-14, which dissolves the near-name) (social standing) is a third, unrelated sense per the false-friend guard on this property's range class. A conversion or census that says standing without naming the sense is wrong by default." .

srd521:engagement a rdf:Property ;
  cat:domainType srd521:AttackIntent ;
  cat:rangeType par:EncounterEngagement ;
  rdfs:label "engagement"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The encounter engagement an attack intent is declared within - the edition intent references the general engagement relator by plain IRI (participatorium owns engagement; combat is one way to be engaged). Property half of the retiring sc:engagement, whose frozen row targeted the relator class alone (the property-to-class case-collapse, wave-4 row 1; the class needed no mint - par:EncounterEngagement is landed). Shape-only origin: the battle-beat contract SHACL and evidence fixtures are its rung." .
